IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dda-core`

-- Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) -- THE DEFENDANT'S SEAT: the person or business sued in a dust disease action (an
-- employer, a manufacturer or supplier of asbestos products), another tortfeasor liable for the same damage, or the
-- insurer sued directly under s 11. A second seat beside the claimant's (dda-seat.l4), drawing on the same rules in
-- dda-core.l4, so the two cannot disagree; each question here has a mirror case in dda-cases-defendant.l4.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (Act version of 1 January 2021;
-- Regulations version of 17 June 2021). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The defendant's questions`

§§ `Contribution (s 4A(3))`
-- Situation: you are liable for damages for a dust disease and want contribution from another person liable for it.

@export I am liable for damages for a dust disease (or a death from one): can I claim contribution from another person liable for the same damage in the South Australian Employment Tribunal (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 4A(3))?
GIVEN `I am a tortfeasor liable for damages for a dust disease or a death from one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a tortfeasor (a wrongdoer) liable for damages for a dust disease, or for the death of a person from one
      `the other person is a tortfeasor liable for the same damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you want contribution from is also a tortfeasor liable for the same damage
GIVETH A `Contribution forum answer`
`Can I claim contribution in SAET` MEANS
    `can the contribution claim go to SAET (s 4A(3))` `I am a tortfeasor liable for damages for a dust disease or a death from one` `the other person is a tortfeasor liable for the same damage`

§§ `Presumed knowledge and exemplary damages (ss 8(2), 9(2))`

@export Am I presumed to have known that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease, because of the kind of business I carried on (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 8(2); Dust Diseases Regulations 2021 reg 4 and Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `my process` IS A `Process` @desc What you were doing at the time: mining or milling of asbestos (or associated packing or transport); manufacture of asbestos products; packing or transport of asbestos products as their manufacturer; sale or supply of asbestos products as their manufacturer; use of asbestos products as their manufacturer; design of an object or thing containing asbestos; sale or other supply of asbestos products not as the manufacturer; installation of asbestos products; use of asbestos products not as the manufacturer; another industrial or commercial process involving asbestos; or a process not involving asbestos
      `the number of persons I employed at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons your business employed at the time of that process
      `the only asbestos was in the structure of my premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another process involving asbestos: whether the only asbestos involved was asbestos in the building or structure where the work happened
      `the day I carried on the process` IS A DATE @desc The day (or the first day) you carried on the process at the time in question
      `it could have exposed another person to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the process could have exposed another person to asbestos dust
      `I prove I did not know` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you prove that you did not know at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease
GIVETH A `Knowledge presumption answer`
`Am I presumed to have known of the danger` MEANS
    `is knowledge presumed (s 8(2))` `my process` `the number of persons I employed at the time` `the only asbestos was in the structure of my premises` `the day I carried on the process` `it could have exposed another person to asbestos dust` `I prove I did not know`

@export Should the court award exemplary (punitive) damages against me in a dust disease action (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 9(2) and s 8(2); Dust Diseases Regulations 2021 regs 4 and 5, Schedules 1 and 2)?
GIVEN `the claimant's disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease the injured person has or had: asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `the claim is a civil action for damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim against you is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `the claimant says my breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant says your breach of a duty owed to the injured person caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the court is satisfied I knew the claimant was at risk of exposure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that you knew the injured person was at risk of exposure to asbestos dust
      `my process` IS A `Process` @desc What you were doing that exposed the injured person (the same list as in the presumed-knowledge question)
      `the number of persons I employed at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons your business employed at the time of that process
      `the only asbestos was in the structure of my premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another process involving asbestos: whether the only asbestos involved was asbestos in the building or structure where the work happened
      `the day of the claimant's exposure` IS A DATE @desc The day (or the first day) of the injured person's exposure to asbestos dust from that process
      `my process resulted in the claimant's exposure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your process resulted in the injured person's exposure to asbestos dust
      `the court is satisfied on the evidence that I knew of the danger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied on the evidence (apart from any presumption) that you knew, at the time of the exposure, that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease
      `I prove I did not know` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you prove that you did not know at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease
GIVETH A `Exemplary damages answer`
`Should exemplary damages be awarded against me` MEANS
    `should exemplary damages be awarded (s 9(2))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the claimant's disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `the claim is a civil action for damages for the disease or a death from it` `the claimant says my breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the court is satisfied I knew the claimant was at risk of exposure` `my process` `the number of persons I employed at the time` `the only asbestos was in the structure of my premises` `the day of the claimant's exposure` `my process resulted in the claimant's exposure` `the court is satisfied on the evidence that I knew of the danger` `I prove I did not know`

§§ `The insurer sued directly (s 11)`
-- Situation: you are the insurer of a defendant who is dead, dissolved, insolvent or cannot be found, and you are sued
-- directly.

@export I am an insurer sued directly in place of the person I insured: what is the most I can be made to pay (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 11(2), (3))?
GIVEN `what the insured would have been liable for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount (in dollars) the person you insured would have been liable to pay had they been sued
      `what I would have had to indemnify` IS A NUMBER @desc The most (in dollars) you would have been liable to pay the person you insured under the policy for that liability
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be made to pay as the insurer` MEANS
    `the insurer's liability (s 11(2), (3))` `what the insured would have been liable for` `what I would have had to indemnify`
